1-6e282fc3-f65e-4de6-9793-7fa2b594819b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"197350cfa7c49feb6b87ff5f9044278535fc9480556974acc4aeeba536fd50e5","event_uuid":"ad5db39b-316d-46ac-b539-51f4436d6c48","position":{"commit_sha":"6d00d2aafeb6960dcbe9ba8d93912646f3bb6f7a","position":"1788375841846320152-ad5db39b-316d-46ac-b539-51f4436d6c48"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d2d7760af2848ee1ad9d3217d6a723a3de58c7402e2cc6b41fd9288e20af4405","event_uuid":"3c7acd47-cd40-497c-a6cb-672fcce40105","position":{"commit_sha":"6a05e7fcd515ac47199156dcb8de2304ecf6a7e1","position":"1788375888500044234-3c7acd47-cd40-497c-a6cb-672fcce40105"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0efbeb972f3dd0caed78b06db0ee6e12d6dc05e005dff92ab59dc7b885c727a9","event_uuid":"4121fd8f-1a3b-4788-9fbb-01fba2cd887a","position":{"commit_sha":"7a6c6c5ffe57a69330c36bb0424f33fc36a158b6","position":"1788376362606970533-4121fd8f-1a3b-4788-9fbb-01fba2cd887a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788375027128681930,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6e282fc3-f65e-4de6-9793-7fa2b594819b","relation":"blocks","target_id":"aa40-cbda-ee38-481c"}],"description":"# S0 — Finalize the Gerrit disk-ceiling ADR\n\n## Why\nThe operator has approved the disk-ceiling architecture, but the durable architectural record has not yet landed. The ADR must capture the approved decision, the recurrence history, and the native-GC/high-watermark precedents before implementation begins.\n\n## What\nCreate `docs/adr/0110-gerrit-disk-ceiling-architecture.md`, create marker `docs/adr/.numbers/0110`, and update `docs/adr/README.md` through `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` if the generated index drifts. Do not change Terraform, host scripts, compose, or runtime behavior in this story.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: ADR text, number marker, ADR index. Out of scope: implementing any disk cap, scratch volume, CloudWatch alarm, or runbook operational change. Those are children of this epic and depend on this ADR story.\n\n## Research findings to cite\n- ADR convention: `docs/adr/README.md` states every numbered ADR owns a marker in `docs/adr/.numbers/`; highest current number is 0109.\n- Infra seams: `infra/terraform/main.tf:27-35`, `:42-64`, `:83-87`; `infra/terraform/user_data.sh:20-70`; `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:233-245`; `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:149-163`; `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py:381`; `src/rebar/review_bot/low_disk.py:69`; `infra/scripts/observability.sh:72-90`; `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:132-140`, `:367-384`, `:410-445`.\n- Recurrence tickets: `2731`, `3a52`, `e4f3`, `3cef`, `3276`, with `/var/gerrit` sibling history `5a05`/`3e92`.\n- External precedents: Kubernetes kubelet image GC high/low thresholds; BuildKit `gc` with `maxUsedSpace`/`minFreeSpace`; Nix `min-free`/`max-free`; journald `SystemMaxUse`/`SystemKeepFree`; systemd-tmpfiles age cleanup and btrfs qgroup helpers; Docker overlay2/container layer docs and `docker container prune --filter until=...`.\n\n## ADR draft text to land\n```md\n# ADR 0110 — Gerrit host disk-ceiling architecture\n\n- **Status:** Draft\n- **Date:** 2026-09-02\n- **Epic:** `endowed-upset-scaup` / `6202-e1c7-c57f-4897`\n- **Supersedes:** N/A\n- **Relates to:** ADR 0005, ADR 0012, ADR 0069, ADR 0077, ADR 0104; incident bugs `2731`, `3a52`, `e4f3`, `3cef`, `3276`, `5a05`, `3e92`.\n\n## Context\nThe single EC2 Gerrit/review-bot host has repeatedly exhausted or nearly exhausted disk. The Sep 2 incident (`3276`) filled the root filesystem and took Gerrit offline for about five hours. Earlier root incidents (`2731`, `3a52`, `e4f3`, `3cef`) show recurrence. Existing mitigations tuned reactive cleanup and alerting but did not impose hard ceilings on Docker overlay2/image layers, Docker build cache, `/var/tmp`, journald, writable container layers, or review gate scratch/clones/snapshots. Keeping root at 60 GiB buys headroom but does not bound any generator.\n\nThe current architecture already keeps Gerrit source-of-truth data on a separate `/var/gerrit` EBS volume (ADR 0012), but review scratch still resolves through tempdir defaults to root because `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` is unset. Current monitoring observes aggregate root and data volume usage, not per-generator cap saturation.\n\n## Decision\nAdopt the operator-approved two-pillar disk-ceiling architecture.\n\n1. **Per-accumulator hard caps on root.** Each residual root consumer gets a native cap or retention bound: Docker/BuildKit GC for image/overlay/build cache, journald `SystemMaxUse`, bounded `/var/tmp` cleanup/quota, and bounded exited-container/writable-layer reaping or runtime quota. Each capped generator also publishes a generator-specific CloudWatch metric and has its own alarm at/near cap.\n2. **Dedicated EBS scratch volume for code-review gates.** Gate snapshots and review clone tempdirs move from root/system temp to an independently sized gp3 volume mounted at a dedicated host path and wired through `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR`/temp configuration. Exhausting review scratch must not exhaust OS/root.\n3. **Keep the 60 GiB root volume as headroom, not as the control.** The correctness property comes from caps and isolation.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n- **Keep resizing root:** rejected because it changes only the denominator; unbounded generators still fill the disk.\n- **One larger shared volume:** rejected because review scratch can still wedge OS/root and generator attribution stays poor.\n- **Only generic root alarm:** rejected because it detects symptoms after pressure, not the saturated generator or a hard cap.\n\n## Consequences\nOperators gain per-generator saturation visibility, and review-gate scratch can fail without taking host OS/root down. Implementation must use Terraform and host Docker/systemd configuration with local/scripted validation, not a CI-provider-specific trigger. It must avoid direct `/var/lib/docker` manipulation except through Docker/BuildKit APIs. `/var/tmp` may need a separate quota-backed path or size-enforcing service because tmpfiles alone primarily supplies age cleanup on XFS.\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] ADR file `docs/adr/0110-gerrit-disk-ceiling-architecture.md` and marker `docs/adr/.numbers/0110` are added.\n- [ ] ADR records the approved Option A + Option C decision without re-litigating it.\n- [ ] ADR cites repo seams, recurrence tickets, and external native-GC precedents listed above.\n- [ ] ADR includes alternatives rejected and consequences, including per-generator alarms and 60 GiB root as non-fix.\n- [ ] This story changes only ADR/index/marker files.\n- [ ] Portability criterion: ADR requires Terraform + host-level Docker/systemd controls and local validation; no GitHub-only CI dependency is introduced.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0110-gerrit-disk-ceiling-architecture.md","reason":"New ADR file for the approved disk-ceiling architecture."},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0110","reason":"New ADR number marker."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"ADR index/category entry if generated index is updated in-tree."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["blocks","aa40-cbda-ee38-481c"],["parent","6202-e1c7-c57f-4897"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"6202-e1c7-c57f-4897","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["infra","gerrit","disk-ceiling","adr"],"ticket_id":"7dfa-18ca-9c04-4691","ticket_type":"story","title":"S0 — Finalize the Gerrit disk-ceiling ADR","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"ADR number marker and index are consistent."},{"command":"git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD | grep -E '^(docs/adr/0110-gerrit-disk-ceiling-architecture\\.md|docs/adr/\\.numbers/0110|docs/adr/README\\.md)$'","dd_id":"AC2","dd_text":"ADR-only story does not change implementation files."}]},"source_event_uuids":["fb21f841-625c-40fc-80ee-7a1d8b0edfdd","ca9dda7e-f5e5-4995-9a7d-c4fa16fbc636","2d14998c-c760-4096-bd6f-5d1f036c94df","6e282fc3-f65e-4de6-9793-7fa2b594819b","ad5db39b-316d-46ac-b539-51f4436d6c48","3c7acd47-cd40-497c-a6cb-672fcce40105","4121fd8f-1a3b-4788-9fbb-01fba2cd887a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788378922803671001,"uuid":"2234eddb-f744-4b6e-bcd2-4f3356129fc0"}